explanation:
Wavenumber $ ar{
u}$ (in $	ext{cm}^{-1}$) is defined as the reciprocal of wavelength: $ ar{
u} =  rac{1}{\lambda}$ where $\lambda$ is in centimetres. For example, $ ar{
u} = 4000 	ext{ cm}^{-1}$ corresponds to $\lambda =  rac{1}{4000} 	ext{ cm} = 2.5 \mu	ext{m}$. Larger wavenumbers (shorter wavelengths) correspond to higher frequencies and higher energies. In IR spectra, the horizontal axis decreases from left ($\sim 4000 	ext{ cm}^{-1}$) to right ($\sim 600 	ext{ cm}^{-1}$).
